ab29c87","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Checkstyle configuration","messageBody":"The project does not automatically check Java source files for coding\nstandard violations.\n\nWithout automated style checks, inconsistent formatting and coding\nstandard violations can be introduced as the codebase grows.\n\nAdd Checkstyle to the Gradle build and provide the required Checkstyle\nand suppression configurations.\n\nAutomating these checks helps keep the codebase consistent and catches\ncoding standard violations during development.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":13,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"e6cd7180006a81a5b36f3cdccff2e73c875167b2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Use varargs for adding dialog boxes","messageBody":"MainWindow adds dialog boxes to the dialog container at several\ndifferent points, with some calls adding one dialog and others adding\nmultiple dialogs.\n\nCalling the container directly in each location duplicates the dialog\naddition logic and makes the intent less explicit.\n\nExtract the repeated operation into an addDialogs method that accepts\na variable number of dialog boxes.\n\nUsing varargs allows the same method to handle both single and multiple\ndialog boxes while keeping the calling code concise.\n","tags":["A-FullCommitMessage"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":137,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"8a70b7d40937fb98b9e5545920d33baa71352076","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix JavaFX GUI integration","messageBody":"Restore the JavaFX launcher, application entry point, dialog box,\nand GUI resources required by MainWindow.\n\nAdd the response API used by the GUI while preserving the existing\nparser, storage, and task behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"gradle":{"insertions":15,"deletions":7},"fxml":{"insertions":74,"deletions":0},"java":{"insertions":336,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"4467ad9e94c2fd62b18785a9a9d36c2583964276","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix Checkstyle violations","messageBody":"Align source and test code with the configured Java coding standard.\nFix formatting, indentation, Javadocs, and abbreviation naming without\nchanging application behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":155,"deletions":142}}}]},{"date":"2026-09-08T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"ef178bf0f53209290e08539b93b483f2fbef1efe","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge pull request #17 from sel-couth-ene/A-CheckStyle-fixes","messageBody":"Fix Checkstyle violations","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}},{"hash":"217e4c65ddca6590cd9c398787f9cc87c21ee3cf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add assertions for task index assumptions","messageBody":"Use Java assertions to document the invariant that task-list\noperations receive valid indexes after input validation.\n\nUpdate the related tests and documentation to reflect assertion\nfailures when internal assumptions are violated.\n","tags":["A-Assertions"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":12,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"2d507cfdde115fe51cdfd063b7f28cfed04b4616","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor duplicated mark logic","messageBody":"Extract the shared task-marking logic used by the CLI and GUI into\na single helper method.\n\nThis removes duplicated parsing, validation, mutation, and storage\ncode while preserving the existing user-facing behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":23,"deletions":21}}},{"hash":"15e148c14fe35fc0ba7429c935b1108265b89c66","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor duplicated unmark logic","messageBody":"Extract the shared task-unmarking logic used by the CLI and GUI into\na single helper method.\n\nThis removes duplicated parsing, validation, mutation, and storage\ncode while preserving the existing user-facing behavior.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":25,"deletions":23}}},{"hash":"514c984574003